{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And because he mentioned a [wild] animal that is not an offering, and likewise a bird, he mentioned <b>any soul that eats a nevelah</b>, which too is not an offering. He also mentioned it on account of the hunt: if intentionally, he transgresses a negative commandment and receives lashes; if unwittingly, he brings a sin-offering. And if one objects: but Scripture says, 'to the stranger who is in your gates you shall give it and he shall eat it' — the answer is that this is a ger toshav, and likewise it is written, 'and the stranger who dwells among you' — he is not abandoned to eat nevelah; rather, the foreigner who comes into our gates, you give it to him and he eats it outside."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:35.581502716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}